<title>USA: TABLE-Western Pacific Air Q2 shr loss $1.56.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Western Pacific Air Q2 shr loss $1.56.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30,</p>
<p>			    1997			   1996</p>
<p> Shr loss	  $	 1.56  profit $	 0.04</p>
<p> Net loss*		 20,924  profit	    521</p>
<p> Revs			43,938		   39,314</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,438		   13,938</p>
<p>	  6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss	  $	 2.90  loss   $	 0.15</p>
<p> Net loss*		 38,961  loss	    1,922</p>
<p> Revs			79,755		   73,019</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,438		   13,248</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Consolidated net loss for second quarter 1997 is $17.669 million, compared with a net income of $521,000 for the same quarter in 1996. The second quarter 1997 net loss includes $2.1 million related to its 57 percent owned subsidiary, Mountain Air Express, and $3.4 million in one-time, nonrecurring charges including certain startup costs in Denver. Mountain Air started flight operations on December 16, 1996.</p>
<p>Consolidated results will not equal the sum of Western Pacific Airlies and Mountain Air Express due to elimination entries and minority interests.</p>
<p>*Attributable to common stock.</p>
<p>Full company name is Western Pacific Airlines Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
